1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:03,520
In China's AI circle this year, there are two most notable post-90s figures

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,480
one is Yao Shunyu

3
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:05,500
born in 1998

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,360
joined Tencent at the end of last year as the Chief AI Scientist

5
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,360
attracted widespread attention

6
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,940
The other is Alibaba's Lin Junyang

7
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:12,000
born in 1993

8
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,620
technical lead of the Qianwen large language model

9
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,000
Now, his departure from Alibaba has sparked industry-wide discussions.

10
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,640
Two post-90s AI leaders, one joining and one leaving

11
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:19,440


12
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,570
The underlying challenge reflected is the same

13
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:23,570
In the AI race where there's no room for failure

14
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:25,990
the ambition of super individuals and the organizational strategy of the company

15
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:27,690
How to reconcile the conflict between the two?

16
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:30,400
To what extent should companies accommodate individual will?

17
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,759
Lin Junyang's resignation has sparked fierce debate

18
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,960
This is Alibaba's old problem resurfacing again, where commercial objectives override technological ideals.

19
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:39,420
Some also believe this was an impulsive move by a tech genius.

20
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:41,000
The 'fragile top student' acts arrogantly due to being spoiled

21
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,400
But what is the truth?

22
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,180
Based on the insider information we've obtained

23
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:45,920
Sort out the details of this resignation incident

24
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:46,720
First, let's talk about Lin Junyang

25
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:47,160
eccentric

26
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:50,640
Unlike Yao Shunyu, who had the upbringing of a 'prodigy' and studied overseas

27
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,640
with international experience including working at OpenAI

28
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,320
Lin Junyang has a background from domestic universities.

29
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:55,940
campus recruit, pure-blood Alibaba employee

30
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:58,420
Some media reported that he graduated from the undergraduate program at Peking University's School of Computer Science.

31
00:00:58,420 --> 00:00:59,380
This is actually a misrepresentation

32
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:02,280
He studied English literature as an undergraduate at the School of International Relations.

33
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:04,920
while simultaneously studying four languages: Japanese, Russian, German, and French

34
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:05,900
was a top liberal arts student

35
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:06,640
during his master's studies

36
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,960
Lin Junyang shifted towards more technical, interdisciplinary fields

37
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,800
studying computational linguistics at Peking University

38
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:13,100
After graduating in 2019, he joined Alibaba DAMO Academy

39
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:15,199
participated in the training of the early Qwen model

40
00:01:15,199 --> 00:01:16,719
In Alibaba's large model team

41
00:01:18,579 --> 00:01:20,979
Initially, the team's technical leader was Yang Hongxia

42
00:01:20,979 --> 00:01:22,560
a renowned scientist in the AI industry

43
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:23,980
She left the company in 2022.

44
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:25,680
later joined ByteDance

45
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,140
The team leader position was taken over by Zhou Chang

46
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,160
Zhou Chang and Lin Junyang share quite similar backgrounds.

47
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:30,900
both are young scientists born in the 1990s

48
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:33,160
also joined Alibaba through campus recruitment after graduating from Peking University

49
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:35,200
But two years later, Zhou Chang also left Alibaba.

50
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,120
Jack Ma once said, there are all kinds of reasons for employees to leave a company

51
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,160
There are only two most genuine reasons

52
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:40,700
either the pay was inadequate

53
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,260
either the 'heart is hurt'

54
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:43,420
The reason for Zhou Chang's resignation

55
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:44,860
According to the information we have obtained

56
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:48,200
First, there was a misalignment between technical judgment and personal interests with the company's direction.

57
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,260
It might have been relatively difficult to secure internally

58
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:51,540
substantial resource support

59
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:53,500
Another reason could be the issue of compensation.

60
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:54,300
Zhou Chang believed that the team's compensation at that time

61
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,220
not sufficiently aligned with market standards

62
00:01:57,220 --> 00:01:58,100
2024

63
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,460
After Zhou Chang was poached by ByteDance

64
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,180
The compensation issues for the Tongyi Qianwen team have seen significant improvement

65
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:04,740
The vacant position of technical lead was taken over by Lin Junyang.

66
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:06,480
Over the past two years under Lin Junyang's leadership

67
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,360
Qianwen large model

68
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,860
has gained greater influence within the global developer community

69
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:10,699
2024

70
00:02:10,699 --> 00:02:12,980
on HuggingFace's model downloads

71
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:13,680
Qianwen ranked first

72
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:14,840
far ahead

73
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:17,160
Based on multiple sources and reports from LatePost

74
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,700
Lin Junyang's management style is

75
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:21,200
prefers to 'stimulate the team's self-drive and cohesion'

76
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:23,360
believes that an ideal manager is someone who is logical

77
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,560
each small team leader

78
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:27,200
The most important thing is to hire people who are better than you.

79
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,240
otherwise, it's 'a complete failure'

80
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,540
Leaders should 'keep their ego small'

81
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:30,800
Don't think you're invincible

82
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,640
can do everything

83
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:33,860
During the years at Alibaba

84
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,240
Lin Junyang is active in

85
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,140
domestic and international social media, promoting the Qwen large model

86
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,580
explain model updates and respond to developer feedback

87
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:41,620
gradually became the soul of Alibaba's large model

88
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:42,480
2025

89
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:45,680
At the age of 32, Lin Junyang became the youngest P10 at Alibaba.

90
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,720
At this stage

91
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:49,680
The Qwen team received relatively positive external evaluations and maintained decent internal morale.

92
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,520
It is precisely because of this

93
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,790
Lin Junyang's resignation shocked everyone.

94
00:02:52,790 --> 00:02:53,710
March 2nd

95
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:55,730
Alibaba just released four new models

96
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:57,070
Musk also gave positive reviews

97
00:02:57,070 --> 00:02:58,190
And the next afternoon

98
00:02:58,190 --> 00:02:59,720
Lin Junyang submitted his resignation

99
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:00,440
the third day

100
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:02,180
Alibaba's management stated at the all-hands meeting

101
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:03,580
The group will try to retain Lin Junyang

102
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:04,880
but individuals should not be deified

103
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:06,840
cannot be retained at all costs and irrationally

104
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:07,500
the fourth day

105
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:08,660
Alibaba issued an internal letter

106
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:10,579
accepted Lin Junyang's resignation application

107
00:03:10,579 --> 00:03:13,119
This marks the most significant change within Alibaba's large model team.

108
00:03:13,119 --> 00:03:15,259
There are both internal, historical legacy issues

109
00:03:15,259 --> 00:03:17,380
as well as the intensifying external competitive landscape

110
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:19,580
the foundational model team led by Lin Junyang

111
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:21,100
was a relatively independent small team

112
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:23,880
Initially, the pursuit was focused on technological influence and contributions to the open-source community.

113
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:26,720
while Alibaba's internal ultimate goal is to achieve AI cloud and AI super applications

114
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:28,940
strategic and business objectives

115
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:32,150
Technical objectives and business objectives are not fully aligned

116
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:35,090
Recently, Alibaba is preparing to restructure the Qianwen team internally.

117
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:37,140
The company formulates strategies and divisions of labor from top to bottom

118
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:39,900
will inevitably create tension with the independent explorations of internal small teams

119
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:41,700
Lin Junyang's scope of management would be reduced

120
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:43,180
directly led to the outbreak of conflict

121
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:45,400
This conflict reflects, in the AI battle,

122
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,310
a common challenge faced by major tech companies

123
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:50,370
Jerry Tworek, an OpenAI veteran, recently said after leaving

124
00:03:50,370 --> 00:03:53,010
OpenAI no longer has the space for high-risk research

125
00:03:53,010 --> 00:03:55,450
All major AI companies are facing multiple pressures

126
00:03:55,450 --> 00:03:56,780
while also driving user growth

127
00:03:56,780 --> 00:03:58,540
while also bearing the high costs of GPUs

128
00:03:58,540 --> 00:03:59,760
and also strive to be first in model development

129
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:02,480
Under these multiple pressures of having to do this, that, and the other

130
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:04,400
the relationship between super individuals and large corporations

131
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:06,030
has become increasingly sensitive and delicate

132
00:04:06,030 --> 00:04:06,690
On one hand

133
00:04:06,690 --> 00:04:09,130
Big tech companies urgently need technical geniuses to drive internal innovation

134
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:11,630
For example, Tencent heavily recruited Yao Shunyu, born in 1998

135
00:04:11,630 --> 00:04:14,500
Upon his arrival, he pointed out that Tencent's large model evaluation had issues.

136
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:16,260
excessive pursuit of rankings on leaderboards

137
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:17,100
excels at answering questions

138
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,540
but the actual performance is not stable

139
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:20,459
demanded the team to stop focusing on leaderboards

140
00:04:20,459 --> 00:04:22,659
Steadfastly focus on building the foundational capabilities of large models

141
00:04:22,659 --> 00:04:25,299
In fact, the original team was not unaware of the issues at hand.

142
00:04:25,299 --> 00:04:26,979
But prolonged collaboration can lead to mutual friction.

143
00:04:26,979 --> 00:04:29,100
A new variable is needed to break the deadlock.

144
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:30,700
Yao Shunyu is just such an "external force"

145
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:32,780
A person involved with the Hunyuan large model told LatePost

146
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:34,760
Completely disrupt the previous rhythm and inertia

147
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,500
is the first step back on track

148
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:37,660
Another manifestation is this

149
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:39,860
the departure controversy of Lin Junyang at Alibaba

150
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:43,200
Frontline AI researchers are the brightest and most self-driven individuals of this era.

151
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,980
while companies emphasize collective goals, demanding strict adherence to directives

152
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:47,420
When individuals with technological ideals

153
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:49,540
when required to compromise for complex strategic objectives

154
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:50,820
conflicts arise

155
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:53,120
To what extent should a company accommodate individual will?

156
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:53,980
There is no standard answer

157
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:56,860
the corporate organization and the young AI technical leads

158
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:58,390
a shared growth challenge

159
00:04:58,390 --> 00:04:59,330
Jack Ma once said

160
00:04:59,330 --> 00:05:01,230
Alibaba should regularly contribute talent to society

161
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:01,930
Coincidentally

162
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:04,390
the previous two technical leaders of Alibaba's large model team

163
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:05,480
were all transferred to ByteDance

164
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:08,200
Currently, Alibaba's entire Tongyi Lab has over 600 employees.

165
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:11,120
ByteDance's model R&D team has over 1,500 members.

166
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,300
The AI battle among tech giants

167
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:15,540
will be a comprehensive battle encompassing technology, products, organization, and talent

168
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:17,560
Lin Junyang's next destination remains unknown

169
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:20,100
But ByteDance has certainly already taken action.

